{"author":"Rebar Bot","author_email":"joeoakhart+bot@navapbc.com","author_id":"594c-9dcf-5ad6-4e6d","author_sig":"{\"payload\": \"\", \"payloadType\": \"application/vnd.rebar.authorship.v1+json\", \"signatures\": [{\"keyid\": \"594c-9dcf-5ad6-4e6d\", \"sig\": \"\"}]}","data":{"body":"Phase 4 decision — RP08 (`S08`, share lifecycle contracts across CLI/library/MCP): REJECTED on 2026-08-30 after explicit ticket, ADR, code, and Git-history review. ADR 0080 already owns schema-derived static public outputs with plain runtime dicts; ADR 0100 owns CLI grammar/help within the CLI boundary; `topaz-blubbery-mice` owns the behavioral write-parity oracle and explicitly chose behavioral conformance over unified/generated adapters; and prior `TransitionRequest` story `ruinable-cozey-caracal` was unparented/closed because CLI-refuse versus library/MCP-discard semantics make convergence a behavior/API decision rather than consolidation. The cited escapes predate that oracle or were encoded as known gaps; no cited post-oracle escape proves the current mitigation failed. Keep three thin facades over shared command behavior, schema-derived static output contracts, and the existing parity oracle. No shared runtime request/result model or admission-behavior convergence is approved by this Janitor pass."},"env_id":"eea68b7f-6697-488b-ac52-744e2ed8e96f","event_type":"COMMENT","timestamp":1788117247199242225,"uuid":"34749329-b102-4221-bc50-200e8d28a2f0"}